<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka benchmark 12-month T-bills ease.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka benchmark 12-month T-bills ease.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of 12-month treasury bills eased by 0.01 percentge points while three-month yields fell by 0.03 percentage points. Six-month yields remained unchanged at Wednesday's auction, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank also said it bought bills worth 165 million rupees.</p>
<p>		   Bids received   Bids accepted   Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     3,690	     2,125	  11.03 (11.06)</p>
<p>    6 months	 663		 240	  11.89 (11.89)</p>
<p>    12 months	836		 570	  12.72 (12.73)</p>
<p>    Total	  5,189		2,935</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
